   0.0338880000 a.u. =    0.9221397934 eV =   7437.55628516 cm-1

 Derivative Coupling before scaling and after scaling

 STEP 1:  Read nacm from output file.
          nacm_x = < \Psi_b | \frac{ \parital H }{ \partial x_{i \alpha} | \Psi_a > / ( E_a - E_b )  (au)

 STEP 2:  Transform the coordinates form x to q.
          nacm_q = < \Psi_b | \frac{ \parital H }{ \partial q_{i \alpha} | \Psi_a > / ( E_a - E_b )  (au)
          where q_{i \alpha} = \sqrt(m_i) * x_{i \alpha}

 STEP 3:  Transform the coordinates form q to normal mode coordinates Q.
          nacm_q = < \Psi_b | \frac{ \parital H }{ \partial Q_j | \Psi_a > / ( E_a - E_b )  (au)

 STEP 4:  Transform the normal mode coordinates Q to dimensionless coordinates Q^\prime.
          nacm_q = < \Psi_b | \frac{ \parital H }{ \partial Q^\prime_j | \Psi_a > / ( E_a - E_b )  (au)
          where Q^\prime = Q * SQRT(w),    and w is the corresponding frequency.

